// Section progression templates. Chords are Roman numerals measured against the MAJOR scale of the
// tonic (so minor-key templates write bIII, bVI, bVII), case gives the triad quality:
//   upper case: "" major, 7 dominant 7, maj7, maj9, 9, 6, add9, sus2, sus4, 7sus4, + augmented
//   lower case: "" minor, 7 minor 7, 9 minor 9, 6 minor 6, o diminished, o7 diminished 7, h7 half-diminished
// Bass: "/3" "/5" "/7" = that chord tone in the bass; "/I", "/bVII"... = that scale degree (pedal or slash).
// ":0.5" scales a chord's length (1 = one harmonic-rhythm slot).
// Columns: id, role, minor?, chords, styles (0 = any), brightness -1..1, tension 0..1, energy 0..1,
//          title, why (one sentence, plain language first, theory term in parentheses), key shift.

